      "body": "### Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes a bug in `compare_perf_reports_pytorch`. `compare_perf_reports_pytorch` merged `ops_summary` sheets on `[\"name\"]` alone. When reports are generated with `--group_by_parent_module` or `is_recompute`, `name` is no longer unique since the report emits one row per `(name, parent_module, is_recompute)` combination, so the outer merge degenerates into a full cross-product.\r\n\r\nThe fix promotes these optional grouping columns into merge keys when they are present in all input reports, and raises an error when some reports have them and others don't.\r\n\r\n### Implementation\r\n\r\n**Root cause.** `SHEETS_COMPARE_CONFIG` defined `ops_summary` merge keys as `[\"name\"]` and did not consider the optional grouping columns:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n\"ops_summary\": {\r\n    \"keys\": [\"name\"],\r\n    ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere are exactly two columns that can make `name` non-unique in `ops_summary`:\r\n\r\n| Column | Trigger |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `parent_module` | `--group_by_parent_module` flag |\r\n| `is_recompute` |  `--detect_recompute` flag |\r\n\r\nIn `process_summary_sheet`, after loading the dataframes, optional keys are promoted to merge keys when present in all input reports. When a key is present in some reports but not all (i.e. comparing a `--group_by_parent_module` report against a non-grouped one), a `ValueError` is raised, since the granularities are incompatible and merging would still produce a partial cross-product.\r\n\r\n### Tests\r\n\r\nThree unit tests in `test_compare_perf_reports.py` using synthetic `ops_summary` CSVs via `tmp_path`:\r\n\r\n| Test | Setup | Assertion |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `test_ops_summary_no_cross_product_with_parent_module` | Both reports have `parent_module`, 2 rows each with duplicate `name` but distinct `parent_module` | Result has 2 rows (not 4), `parent_module` in output columns |\r\n| `test_ops_summary_merge_without_parent_module` | Neither report has `parent_module`, 2 rows each with unique `name` | Result has 2 rows, `parent_module` not in output columns |\r\n| `test_ops_summary_mismatched_parent_module_raises` | One report has `parent_module`, the other doesn't | `ValueError` raised matching `\"parent_module\"` |\r\n\r\nAll three tests verified to fail on the original code and pass on the fix.\r\n\r\nCloses #1014",
